{
  "_source": "Our own table: the recipes of UHV's Proxima life (docs/eras/uhv.md, machines 12, 26, 27, 28 and 30; lines 13, 14 and 15; package UHV-B4). Real practice behind each step: Mars Sample Return's receiving facility (NASA/ESA), far-red photosynthesis with chlorophyll f (Chen, 2010; Kiang et al., 2007), Dsup-like radioprotective proteins (Hashimoto, 2016), fungal chitosan by deacetylation, and Cladosporium sphaerospermum's radiotrophic growth and melanin shielding (Shunk et al., 2020, ISS).",
  "_how_it_is_used": [
    "Read by server_scripts/grindless/uhv/proxima_life.js at every server load. Each entry becomes one recipe of its type, id grindless:<type>/<name> (GTM's builder puts the type in front); our types carry the data key of the type = <name> (the EMI line).",
    "site: 'proxima_b' runs only on gcyr:proxima_centauri_b (G.places), 'earth' only in minecraft:overworld; no site: anywhere (the GTM rows).",
    "itemsIn / itemsOut: { id, count, chance? } (chance in 1/10,000; below 10,000 a chanced input or output of 1); kept: items not used up; fluidsIn / fluidsOut: { id, amount } in mB.",
    "One recipe per lookup path: the circuit is the step on our types; no recipe of a type takes a subset of another's ingredients (checked at load). GTM rows (circuit 0) are keyed by our own items.",
    "Destinations: the biomass the plants and the vat leave is MV's biorefinery's; the salt water from the caustic steps goes to GTM's electrolyser; the extracts on Earth go to GTM's centrifuge (biomass, water and CO2); the oxygen is the base's air."
  ],
